Current list of drivers to be implemented and the status of re-implementation
=============================================================================

Guest packaging uses `rbuild kernel` / `rbuild kerneldrivers` with the profile
architecture. On the current ppc build box, only `drivers-ppc` optional drivers
are scanned; i386 projects are out of scope until an i386 profile run. WIP
paths live in `src/rbuild-1/kernel-drivers-blacklist.json` and are skipped until
promoted out of that list.

bus
All five bus drivers now build with `make` exit 0 for i386 and boot-test clean
under QEMU `-M pc`, each grafted one at a time into its own copy of the golden
image alongside the rebuilt i386 kernel. "Boot-tested" below means the kernel
reached its userland handoff (`Power management is enabled.`) with no panic,
trap or debugger entry on the serial console, and the run matched a control
boot of the same image with Apple's own driver in place. Retested 2026-09-20
against the current rebuilt kernel: all five now carry the boot past
`Configuring device drivers` and through to the Rhapsody Setup Assistant at
800x600, the five GUI frames pixel-identical to one another, and each driver
reproduces its documented behaviour below - PCI enumeration for drvPCIBus, the
duplicate PCMCIA0 for drvPCMCIABus, silent declines for Intel824X0 and PCIC.
The earlier note here that the machine never reached a login window, stalling at
`Configuring device drivers`, described the stock kernel, which in fact dies
earlier still in the open EIDE defect; it no longer holds. Controls with Apple's
own drivers were not re-run on that date. drvPCIBus and drvEISABus were also
booted together in one image, both binaries hash-verified in place beforehand:
they coexist, EISA0 registers, PCI enumeration still resolves the display at
bus 0 dev 2 func 0, and the desktop is pixel-identical to the PCIBus-only run.
None are hardware-tested.

 * drvEISABus - reconstructed against the reference binary, PnPDump 45/186 functions byte-identical with 96 hand-written leftovers accepted in the PnPDump ledger (compiler-shaped / stub / dual-bar), EISABus_reloc shared PnP class methods 53/93 identical or masked-eq; builds clean and boot-tested, registers EISA0 and survives a PnP BIOS that answers PNPB_R_FUNCTION_NOT_SUPPORTED. Diverges from Apple's binary in PnP read port (0x277 against Apple's 0x0)
 * drvPCIBus - reconstructed against the reference binary, fixes applied; its testIDs:dev:fun:bus: prototype now matches Apple's, and PCIResourceDriver inherits IODirectDevice; builds clean and boot-tested, registers PCI0 and enumerates every PCI device, serial output identical to the control
 * drvPCMCIABus - reconstructed against the reference binary, fixes applied; protocol records, every class instance size and ivar layout are byte-identical to the reference; two heap overflows from undeclared ivars fixed; builds clean and boot-tested. Registers PCMCIA0 twice - a duplicate instantiation, not yet explained, and not an artefact of the synthesised Instance0.table
 * Intel824X0PCI - reconstructed against the reference binary, fixes applied; builds clean and boot-tested. Loads and declines silently under QEMU, whose host bridge is 8086:1237 and not one of the 82434LX/NX IDs it auto-detects, so its probe path is untested
 * Intel82365PCMCIA - reconstructed against the reference binary, all fixes applied; its five ObjC protocol records and four adoptions are byte-identical to the reference; builds clean and boot-tested, probes 0x3e0, reports no device and declines cleanly. QEMU has no PCMCIA bridge, so the attach path is untested

ide
 * drvAHCI - newly written rather than reconstructed: Rhapsody predates AHCI, so no Apple reference binary exists. Tested working - boots to userland under QEMU q35 on the built-in ICH9 SATA controller (8086:2922), with both ports detecting their disks, hd0/hd1 registering and root mounting over AHCI. Needs the UEFI loader's PCI config-mechanism report to bind; Not yet tested on hardware
 * drvEIDE - refactored, now with VIA, AMD, and Intel PIIX to ICH4 specific code; not yet tested
 * drvPCFloppy - reconstructed against Apple's Floppy_reloc; not yet tested on hardware

input
 * drvBusMouse - compiles; 7/11 hand-written functions masked-equal to BusMouse_reloc, apple-generic version objects emitted; not yet tested on hardware
 * drvISASerialPort - needs compiled and then tested
 * drvPCParallel - compiles; reconstructed against the reference binary, 40/75 reloc functions byte-identical, 17 masked-equal, remainder accepted compiler-shaped; both tools rebuilt and compared; not yet tested
 * drvPS2Keyboard - compiles; reconstructed against the reference binary, 34/47 hand-written functions byte-identical under relocation masking, remainder accepted as compiler-shaped; not yet tested
 * drvPS2Mouse - compiles; 6/11 hand-written functions masked-equal to PS2Mouse_reloc, five compiler-shaped leftovers accepted, SGS VERS_STRING/VERS_NUM unmet (guest lacks next-sgs.make); not yet tested on hardware
 * drvSerialPointingDevice - compiles; reconstructed against the reference binary, 10/16 hand-written functions byte-identical under relocation masking, remainder accepted as compiler-shaped; Kernel Server vers_string objects still unmet on this guest; not yet tested

